-- #5007 (release 2 of #4918): sections 5 and 6 of the untouched starter privacy
-- body list every member-facing recipient in the register and name the host
-- through {{data-hosting}}. Only a body still byte-for-byte #4914's text, or
-- #4031's before it (which an old bundle or a stale editor save can restore),
-- changes; an edited page keeps every byte. The header date moves only on a
-- starter header. Needs the #4918 release serving: older code shows the token
-- as raw braces; see UPGRADING.
UPDATE "PageContent"
SET "contentHtml" = $cms$<div class="website-legal-copy">
<div><h2>1. Who We Are</h2><p>The {{club-name}} Incorporated (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is a not-for-profit incorporated society registered in New Zealand. We operate {{lodge-name}} and this booking and membership management system (&ldquo;the System&rdquo;).</p><p>We are committed to protecting your personal information and complying with the <strong>New Zealand Privacy Act 2020</strong> and its 13 Information Privacy Principles (IPPs).</p></div>
<div><h2>2. What Information We Collect</h2><p>We collect the following categories of personal information:</p><ul><li><strong>Identity and contact details:</strong> Title, first and last name, email address, phone number, date of birth, gender, occupation, street and postal addresses.</li><li><strong>Profile and stay details:</strong> Profile photos and any dietary or allergy information you provide, including for individual stays.</li><li><strong>Account credentials:</strong> Hashed password (we never store your password in plain text), verification and sign-in records, two-factor authentication settings and secrets, and linked sign-in account identifiers.</li><li><strong>Booking information:</strong> Dates of stay, guest names and age groups, member/non-member status.</li><li><strong>Payment information:</strong> Payment status, Stripe payment reference IDs. We do <em>not</em> store full card numbers &mdash; payment card data is handled directly by Stripe.</li><li><strong>Membership information:</strong> Membership subscription status, season year, Xero invoice references, membership dates and history, family relationships, roles and lodge induction or hosting eligibility, account preferences and consent choices, and administrative notes and reasons for membership changes.</li><li><strong>Chore roster data:</strong> Chore assignments linked to your lodge stays.</li><li><strong>Communication records:</strong> Emails sent to you by the system (booking confirmations, reminders, notifications).</li><li><strong>System usage logs:</strong> IP addresses and request logs for security and troubleshooting purposes.</li></ul><p>We collect only the information necessary for managing club membership and lodge bookings (IPP 1 &mdash; Purpose of collection).</p></div>
<div><h2>3. How We Collect Information</h2><p>We collect your information:</p><ul><li>Directly from you when you register an account, make a booking, or contact us.</li><li>From Xero, our accounting platform, when we import membership and subscription information.</li><li>Automatically through the System when you log in and use the booking features.</li></ul><p>Where we collect information from you, we will tell you why we are collecting it at the point of collection (IPP 3 &mdash; Collection of information from subject).</p></div>
<div><h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2><p>We use your personal information to:</p><ul><li>Create and manage your member account.</li><li>Process and manage lodge bookings.</li><li>Process payments and issue refunds through Stripe.</li><li>Manage membership subscriptions and invoicing through Xero.</li><li>Send you booking confirmations, reminders, and other transactional emails.</li><li>Assign chore roster duties during your lodge stays.</li><li>Maintain financial and membership records as required by law.</li><li>Ensure the security and integrity of the System.</li></ul><p>We will only use your information for the purposes for which it was collected, or for directly related purposes (IPP 10 &mdash; Limits on use of personal information).</p></div>
<div><h2>5. Who We Share Your Information With</h2><p>We share your personal information with the service providers below where necessary to operate the System. A service marked &ldquo;Only if the club turns it on&rdquo; receives nothing unless the club has switched it on.</p><ul><li><strong>Hosting provider</strong> &mdash; Runs the System and stores its database, uploaded files and server logs, which include your personal information. {{data-hosting}}</li><li><strong>Amazon S3 (database backups)</strong> &mdash; Compressed copies of the database, stored in Amazon S3 with restricted access. Only if the club turns it on. See <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS Privacy Notice</a>.</li><li><strong>Email service</strong> &mdash; Delivers the System&rsquo;s emails, so it receives your name, email address and each message, which can include booking details and sign-in links. The club uses either Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) or its own email relay. See <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS Privacy Notice</a>.</li><li><strong>Stripe</strong> &mdash; Payment processing. Stripe receives payment amounts, the payer&rsquo;s email address and booking or subscription references. Card details go from your browser directly to Stripe. See <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Xero</strong> &mdash; Accounting and invoicing. Your contact details and accounting records, including invoice, payment and subscription references, are kept in step with Xero. See <a href="https://www.xero.com/about/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Xero&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Google</strong> &mdash; Website analytics (Google Analytics 4) and Google sign-in. Analytics loads only after you accept analytics cookies and receives usage events and browser and device details, not your name or email address. If you choose to sign in with Google, Google exchanges your identity details with the System. Only if the club turns it on. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Anthropic</strong> &mdash; The AI help assistant and AI Diagnostics. The assistant receives your questions, the conversation and the page context it is allowed to use. AI Diagnostics receives officers&rsquo; troubleshooting questions and the records they look up, which can include your personal information. Only if the club turns it on. See <a href="https://privacy.anthropic.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anthropic&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Sentry</strong> &mdash; Error reporting. Sentry receives error reports and diagnostic details, filtered to reduce personal information, and, if the club also turns on session replay, masked recordings of how a page was used. Only if the club turns it on. See <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sentry&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Have I Been Pwned</strong> &mdash; Checks whether a new password has appeared in a known data breach. It receives only the first five characters of a scrambled (hashed) form of the password, never the password itself or who you are. On unless the club turns it off. See <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/Privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Have I Been Pwned&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Addy</strong> &mdash; Address lookup. Addy receives the address you type while searching and the address you pick. Only if the club turns it on. See <a href="https://www.addysolutions.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Addy&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Video-meeting server</strong> &mdash; Video meetings, run on a meeting server the club chooses. It receives your display name and network details and, when you join a meeting, your audio and video. Only if the club turns it on.</li><li><strong>Alpine Central Server</strong> &mdash; Shares the club&rsquo;s lodge listings and the booking officer&rsquo;s contact details with other connected clubs. No member list is uploaded. Only if the club turns it on.</li></ul><p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to any third party for marketing or other unrelated purposes (IPP 11 &mdash; Limits on disclosure of personal information).</p><p>The System does not fix the country in which any of these providers processes information; that depends on the provider and on the club&rsquo;s account with it, so your information may be processed outside New Zealand. Where we disclose information to a provider outside New Zealand, we take reasonable steps to ensure it is required to protect the information consistently with the Privacy Act 2020 (IPP 12 &mdash; Disclosure of information outside New Zealand).</p><p><strong>Admin note:</strong> Fill in <em>Where members&rsquo; data is held</em> under Club Identity so the hosting entry names your provider and location, and check this list against the services your club uses.</p></div>
<div><h2>6. How We Store and Protect Your Information</h2><ul><li>Your information is stored in a PostgreSQL database run by the hosting provider named in section 5.</li><li>Passwords are hashed using bcrypt before storage &mdash; we cannot see your password.</li><li>Stored credentials for connected services (such as the club&rsquo;s Xero connection) are encrypted using AES-256-GCM before storage.</li><li>All communication between your browser and our servers uses HTTPS.</li><li>We use security headers (Content Security Policy, HSTS, etc.) to protect against common web attacks.</li></ul><p>We take reasonable steps to protect your personal information from unauthorised access, disclosure, or misuse (IPP 5 &mdash; Storage and security of personal information).</p></div>
<div><h2>7. How Long We Keep Your Information</h2><ul><li><strong>Active member accounts:</strong> Retained for as long as you remain a member or have an active account.</li><li><strong>Booking and payment records:</strong> Retained for 7 years as required by New Zealand tax law (Income Tax Act 2007).</li><li><strong>Email logs:</strong> {{email-log-retention}}.</li><li><strong>System audit logs</strong> (a record of who did what in the booking system, including the IP address and browser of the person acting). How long an entry is normally kept depends on its kind:<ul><li>Routine diagnostic entries: deleted after 90 days.</li><li>Records of access to sensitive information: kept for 2 years, or up to 7 years if the club keeps an audit archive.</li><li>Records of changes to accounts, bookings and payments, security events, and routine system records: kept for 7 years.</li></ul>Two rules apply to every kind: IP address and browser details are removed from entries after 90 days, and an entry kept as evidence of an incident is kept, with its IP address and browser details, for at least 10 years.</li><li><strong>Password reset and verification tokens:</strong> Automatically deleted after use or expiry (1&ndash;24 hours).</li></ul><p>We do not keep personal information for longer than is necessary for the purpose for which it was collected (IPP 9 &mdash; Retention of personal information).</p></div>
<div><h2>8. Your Rights</h2><p>Under the Privacy Act 2020, you have the right to:</p><ul><li><strong>Access your information (IPP 6):</strong> Request a copy of the personal information we hold about you. You can download your data from your <a href="/profile">Profile page</a>.</li><li><strong>Correct your information (IPP 7):</strong> Request that inaccurate information be corrected. You can update your profile details directly, or contact us for assistance.</li><li><strong>Request deletion:</strong> Request deletion of your account and personal data from your Profile page. Note that some financial records must be retained for legal compliance.</li><li><strong>Complain:</strong> If you believe we have breached the Privacy Act 2020, you may complain to us first, or directly to the <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Office of the Privacy Commissioner</a>.</li></ul></div>
<div><h2>9. Cookies and Tracking</h2><p>This System uses a session cookie to keep you logged in. This cookie contains an encrypted session token and no personal information. If the club enables Google Analytics, we ask for your consent before loading GA4 analytics cookies. Consent Mode starts with analytics storage denied; GA4 loads only after you accept and is used for aggregate site-use reporting, not advertising. You can decline and keep using the System. The session cookie expires after 8 hours of inactivity or when you sign out.</p><p><strong>Admin note:</strong> Review this section before enabling the Analytics module for your club.</p></div>
<div><h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page. Continued use of the System after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p></div>
<div><h2>11. Contact Our Privacy Officer</h2><p>For any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, or to exercise your privacy rights, please contact our Privacy Officer:</p><div class="website-legal-callout"><p><strong>Privacy Officer</strong></p><p>{{club-name}} Incorporated</p><p>Please use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.</p></div></div>
</div>$cms$,
    "headerText" = CASE
      WHEN "headerText" IN ('How we collect, use, and protect your personal information.<br><small>Effective 1 April 2026 &mdash; Last updated 12 November 2026</small>', 'How we collect, use, and protect your personal information.<br><small>Effective 1 April 2026 &mdash; Last updated 17 October 2026</small>')
      THEN 'How we collect, use, and protect your personal information.<br><small>Effective 1 April 2026 &mdash; Last updated 15 November 2026</small>'
      ELSE "headerText"
    END,
    "updatedAt" = timezone('UTC', statement_timestamp())
WHERE "slug" = 'privacy'
  AND "contentHtml" IN ($previous$<div class="website-legal-copy">
<div><h2>1. Who We Are</h2><p>The {{club-name}} Incorporated (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, &ldquo;our&rdquo;) is a not-for-profit incorporated society registered in New Zealand. We operate {{lodge-name}} and this booking and membership management system (&ldquo;the System&rdquo;).</p><p>We are committed to protecting your personal information and complying with the <strong>New Zealand Privacy Act 2020</strong> and its 13 Information Privacy Principles (IPPs).</p></div>
<div><h2>2. What Information We Collect</h2><p>We collect the following categories of personal information:</p><ul><li><strong>Identity and contact details:</strong> Title, first and last name, email address, phone number, date of birth, gender, occupation, street and postal addresses.</li><li><strong>Profile and stay details:</strong> Profile photos and any dietary or allergy information you provide, including for individual stays.</li><li><strong>Account credentials:</strong> Hashed password (we never store your password in plain text), verification and sign-in records, two-factor authentication settings and secrets, and linked sign-in account identifiers.</li><li><strong>Booking information:</strong> Dates of stay, guest names and age groups, member/non-member status.</li><li><strong>Payment information:</strong> Payment status, Stripe payment reference IDs. We do <em>not</em> store full card numbers &mdash; payment card data is handled directly by Stripe.</li><li><strong>Membership information:</strong> Membership subscription status, season year, Xero invoice references, membership dates and history, family relationships, roles and lodge induction or hosting eligibility, account preferences and consent choices, and administrative notes and reasons for membership changes.</li><li><strong>Chore roster data:</strong> Chore assignments linked to your lodge stays.</li><li><strong>Communication records:</strong> Emails sent to you by the system (booking confirmations, reminders, notifications).</li><li><strong>System usage logs:</strong> IP addresses and request logs for security and troubleshooting purposes.</li></ul><p>We collect only the information necessary for managing club membership and lodge bookings (IPP 1 &mdash; Purpose of collection).</p></div>
<div><h2>3. How We Collect Information</h2><p>We collect your information:</p><ul><li>Directly from you when you register an account, make a booking, or contact us.</li><li>From Xero, our accounting platform, when we import membership and subscription information.</li><li>Automatically through the System when you log in and use the booking features.</li></ul><p>Where we collect information from you, we will tell you why we are collecting it at the point of collection (IPP 3 &mdash; Collection of information from subject).</p></div>
<div><h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2><p>We use your personal information to:</p><ul><li>Create and manage your member account.</li><li>Process and manage lodge bookings.</li><li>Process payments and issue refunds through Stripe.</li><li>Manage membership subscriptions and invoicing through Xero.</li><li>Send you booking confirmations, reminders, and other transactional emails.</li><li>Assign chore roster duties during your lodge stays.</li><li>Maintain financial and membership records as required by law.</li><li>Ensure the security and integrity of the System.</li></ul><p>We will only use your information for the purposes for which it was collected, or for directly related purposes (IPP 10 &mdash; Limits on use of personal information).</p></div>
<div><h2>5. Who We Share Your Information With</h2><p>We share your personal information with service providers where necessary; the following entries apply only to services the club uses to operate the System:</p><ul><li><strong>Stripe Inc.</strong> &mdash; Payment processing. Stripe receives payment card details and processes transactions on our behalf. Stripe is PCI-DSS compliant. See <a href="https://stripe.com/en-nz/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe's Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Xero Limited</strong> &mdash; Accounting and invoicing. Your name, email, and membership subscription status are synchronised with Xero to manage invoices and verify membership. Xero is headquartered in New Zealand. See <a href="https://www.xero.com/nz/about/policies/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Xero's Privacy Policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS) &mdash; Simple Email Service (SES)</strong> &mdash; Transactional email delivery. Your email address is used to send you booking confirmations and notifications. AWS SES operates within AWS's secure infrastructure. See <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS Privacy Notice</a>.</li><li><strong>Hosting and backup providers</strong> &mdash; The providers chosen by the club store the application database and any configured backups.</li><li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> &mdash; Optional aggregate website analytics. GA4 loads only when the club enables the Analytics module and you accept analytics cookies. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li></ul><p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to any third party for marketing or other unrelated purposes (IPP 11 &mdash; Limits on disclosure of personal information).</p><p>Where we disclose information to the overseas providers listed above, we take reasonable steps to ensure those recipients are required to protect the information consistently with the Privacy Act 2020 (IPP 12 &mdash; Disclosure of information outside New Zealand).</p><p><strong>Admin note:</strong> Check this list against the integrations your club actually uses. Name your hosting provider, region, backup store and recipients; remove unused services and add any others receiving personal information.</p></div>
<div><h2>6. How We Store and Protect Your Information</h2><ul><li>Your data is stored in a PostgreSQL database run by the club's hosting provider.</li><li>Passwords are hashed using bcrypt before storage &mdash; we cannot see your password.</li><li>Sensitive tokens (such as Xero OAuth tokens) are encrypted using AES-256-GCM before storage.</li><li>All communication between your browser and our servers uses HTTPS with automatic TLS certificates.</li><li>Where database backups are configured, access to them is restricted.</li><li>We use security headers (Content Security Policy, HSTS, etc.) to protect against common web attacks.</li></ul><p>We take reasonable steps to protect your personal information from unauthorised access, disclosure, or misuse (IPP 5 &mdash; Storage and security of personal information).</p><p><strong>Admin note:</strong> Name your hosting provider, region, backup store and any other recipients. Describe your actual backup arrangements, including whether backups are encrypted, or state if backups are not configured.</p></div>
<div><h2>7. How Long We Keep Your Information</h2><ul><li><strong>Active member accounts:</strong> Retained for as long as you remain a member or have an active account.</li><li><strong>Booking and payment records:</strong> Retained for 7 years as required by New Zealand tax law (Income Tax Act 2007).</li><li><strong>Email logs:</strong> {{email-log-retention}}.</li><li><strong>System audit logs</strong> (a record of who did what in the booking system, including the IP address and browser of the person acting). How long an entry is normally kept depends on its kind:<ul><li>Routine diagnostic entries: deleted after 90 days.</li><li>Records of access to sensitive information: kept for 2 years, or up to 7 years if the club keeps an audit archive.</li><li>Records of changes to accounts, bookings and payments, security events, and routine system records: kept for 7 years.</li></ul>Two rules apply to every kind: IP address and browser details are removed from entries after 90 days, and an entry kept as evidence of an incident is kept, with its IP address and browser details, for at least 10 years.</li><li><strong>Password reset and verification tokens:</strong> Automatically deleted after use or expiry (1&ndash;24 hours).</li></ul><p>We do not keep personal information for longer than is necessary for the purpose for which it was collected (IPP 9 &mdash; Retention of personal information).</p></div>
<div><h2>8. Your Rights</h2><p>Under the Privacy Act 2020, you have the right to:</p><ul><li><strong>Access your information (IPP 6):</strong> Request a copy of the personal information we hold about you. You can download your data from your <a href="/profile">Profile page</a>.</li><li><strong>Correct your information (IPP 7):</strong> Request that inaccurate information be corrected. You can update your profile details directly, or contact us for assistance.</li><li><strong>Request deletion:</strong> Request deletion of your account and personal data from your Profile page. Note that some financial records must be retained for legal compliance.</li><li><strong>Complain:</strong> If you believe we have breached the Privacy Act 2020, you may complain to us first, or directly to the <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Office of the Privacy Commissioner</a>.</li></ul></div>
<div><h2>9. Cookies and Tracking</h2><p>This System uses a session cookie to keep you logged in. This cookie contains an encrypted session token and no personal information. If the club enables Google Analytics, we ask for your consent before loading GA4 analytics cookies. Consent Mode starts with analytics storage denied; GA4 loads only after you accept and is used for aggregate site-use reporting, not advertising. You can decline and keep using the System. The session cookie expires after 8 hours of inactivity or when you sign out.</p><p><strong>Admin note:</strong> Review this section before enabling the Analytics module for your club.</p></div>
<div><h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page. Continued use of the System after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p></div>
<div><h2>11. Contact Our Privacy Officer</h2><p>For any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, or to exercise your privacy rights, please contact our Privacy Officer:</p><div class="website-legal-callout"><p><strong>Privacy Officer</strong></p><p>{{club-name}} Incorporated</p><p>Please use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.</p></div></div>
